ARM: dts: qcom: apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo: mux the WCN3660 Bluetooth pins

Risk: LOW. Needs CONFIG_BT_QCOMSMD (see CONFIG-CHANGES.txt).

The "qcom,wcnss-bt" node already exists in qcom-apq8064.dtsi and is enabled
with riva; the vendor kernel uses the same transport (flo_defconfig:
CONFIG_BT_HCISMD=y; device/asus/flo ueventd.flo.rc: /dev/smd2, /dev/smd3 owned
by bluetooth). Add the riva_bt pin function on GPIO 16/17 as the mako and
yuga boards do.

Not verified from flo sources: the vendor gpiomux tables do not list GPIO
16/17 at all (function 1 = riva_bt is presumably left as set by the
bootloader), so this hunk follows the sibling boards rather than flo data.
The controller has no address until one is set ("btmgmt public-addr" or a
local-bd-address property).
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts
index 1ed6d67..4ca46ed 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-apq8064-asus-nexus7-flo.dts
@@ -409,10 +409,10 @@
 	};
 };
 
-/* Qualcomm WCN3660 Wi-Fi. */
+/* Qualcomm WCN3660 Wi-Fi and Bluetooth (HCI over SMD). */
 &riva {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
-	pinctrl-0 = <&riva_wlan_pin_a>;
+	pinctrl-0 = <&riva_wlan_pin_a>, <&riva_bt_pin_a>;
 	vddcx-supply = <&pm8921_s3>;
 	vddmx-supply = <&pm8921_l24>;
 	vddpx-supply = <&pm8921_s4>;
